<p>
  As shown in the heatmap, there is a clear diagonal transition boundary. As the task frequency decreases, learning requires larger and larger models. The representations of the larger models were evaluated using Distributed Alignment Search (DAS), which confirmed that the causal features (order and Fourier modes) were explicitly encoded in the representations of the large models, but absent in the small models.
</p>
</section>

